  "name": "worktrees",
  "description": "This skill should be used when git worktrees break across a sandbox or container and its host: you are running in a sandbox, container or VM that mounts the repository from the host; git says `.git file does not reference a repository`; a worktree is missing or `git worktree list` marks it prunable; the host (desktop app, IDE, the user's own git) cannot open a worktree an agent made; or the SessionStart context asks about relative worktree links. Covers enabling and undoing relative worktree links, why never to prune, and how to reinstate a pruned worktree.",
